    "verdict": "CIRCULAR — GAP-A-1 reduces to Δ_λ. Substrate-only data (q_0, χ^λ, y_λ, nucleon braids) DOES uniquely fix the binding operator K = σ_3^2 for ²H (PSD-feasible, Markov-fingerprint matched, NO B_AME). But K's per-block content is its CHARACTER χ^λ(K) — a dimensionless Hecke trace. The per-isotope binding requires the mass-functor per-block component M_λ(K) (MeV), and Δ_λ(K) = (M_λ − m_e y_λ χ^λ)/(m_e y_λ χ^λ). Knowing χ^λ(K) does NOT determine M_λ(K): the only available map χ^λ → M_λ (per_block_phi_q.fit_three_E0) FITS per-block energy scales E_0^λ to {e⁻, p, n}. The deuteron binding equation is 1 equation in p(6)=11 unknowns Δ_λ — underdetermined without an external M_λ-source (equivalently B_AME). So GAP-A-1's binding-K leg supplies the SAME χ^λ data #1592 showed is insufficient, and fixing M_λ from K is exactly the open Δ_λ(K) problem. GAP-A-1 ⊆ Δ_λ."
  },
